      "id": 11389,
      "name": "tzgardner",
      "username": "tzgardner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/b77776/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-10-12T05:27:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Curious if there were any rules for searching your deck or trash?</p><p>So, lets say I played Instrumental Conjuration from Argent Adept's deck.</p><blockquote><p>Search your deck or trash for an instrument card and put it into play.</p></blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Can I look through my deck and decide I don't want any of the instruments in there and then take one from the trash (or vice versa) instead? &nbsp;Or is there a rule that says that if I start to look through my deck I must take a card from the deck instead of the trash?</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:41.344Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
