    {
      "id": 119157,
      "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-10-12T12:04:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The only potential issue is if your deck is stacked; if not, there's no harm in flicking through your deck and then shuffling it without taking an instrument, but if it is stacked it's a bit problematic. Of course, you can always just take out the cards that need to be on top/bottom, shuffle, and then restack, so it still works well enough, it's just fiddly. (This is, of course, if you assume that 'deck or trash' means that if you're taking from the trash you can't officially have searched your deck, and thus can't officially shuffle it.)</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:52:16.694Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
