      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>The only potential issue is if your deck is stacked; if not, there&#39;s no harm in flicking through your deck and then shuffling it without taking an instrument, but if it is stacked it&#39;s a bit problematic. Of course, you can always just take out the cards that need to be on top/bottom, shuffle, and then restack, so it still works well enough, it&#39;s just fiddly. (This is, of course, if you assume that &#39;deck or trash&#39; means that if you&#39;re taking from the trash you can&#39;t officially have searched your deck, and thus can&#39;t officially shuffle it.)</p>",
