      "created_at": "2014-10-12T15:13:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Trash is public information. You can just look at your trash before declaring what you're searching.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Spiff has some nifty search cards that tell you all the card you can pick out of deck/trash, so you can decide beforehand which you want. They help a lot.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In case anyone is interested (because Silverleaf is - as usual - right, these are <strong><em>very </em></strong>useful), <a href=\"http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/files/search_sheets.zip\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">the search cards</a> are available from <a href=\"http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/printable.cfm\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">the \"Print and Play\" page</a> on <a href=\"http://www.spiffworld.com/sotm/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Spiff's SotM site</a>.</p>",
